L-NS-14 in POLICY-NO-SHOW version 3 and no such evidence id, and his own device track contradicts him: across the whole window his device sits between 715.46 m and 722.44 m from the pin, stationary at 0.0 km/h, with 0 fixes inside the 150 m LARGE_VENUE rider-presence radius. POL-NS-04 (rider contact unanswered by the driver) cannot exonerate him. I accept, for the sake of argument, that his 18:43:45 message 'coming down now' was coordinating content and that the driver neither replied within 120 seconds (his only message, 'hi im at the pickup point, where are you', was sent at 18:41:50, before the rider's) nor made an in-app call (trip_record.in_app_calls is empty), so limbs (a) and (b) are met. Limb (c), however, is affirmatively failed on his own admissible fixes - POL-NS-04 requires the rider within 150 m for the majority of qualifying fixes - so that clause does not apply and the dispute is decided under POL-NS-01. POL-NS-11 does not assist either, because the rider track is present and complete rather than absent or wholly filtered. POL-NS-06 gives no refund: the dwell exceeded the waiting period instead of falling short, and the missing advisory EV-ADVIS-03109-01 (status MISSING, weight 0.0) is immaterial because the driver does not need the limb (i) accumulation route. On the payment-state point: yes, NO_ACTION would leave the SGD 4.50 with the platform, but that is not the outcome here - the charge is supported on the evidence and stands, and the money this ruling moves is the driver's compensation.\n\nNO ESCALATION. Every artifact that bears on arrival, dwell and rider presence - EV-TRIP-03109, EV-GPS-03109, EV-CHAT-03109 - is COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, and the fare line reconciles to the fee in force, so nothing is impaired under POL-NS-08(a) to (d) and POL-NS-09(e) is not engaged; the trip record's 6.3-minute wait and the trace's 380-second run agree rather than contradict. rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d, rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d are all 0, so POL-NS-09(c) and (d) are not met. The profiles are used for nothing else: the referee flagged the reference to the lifetime counter prior_no_show_flags, and it was cited only to say it may not be substituted for the trailing-30-day figure - no finding rests on any context-only profile field (POL-GEN-01). The referee discarded no claim from either side, and I have discarded none.\n\nTHE OUTCOME. Because POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's payout at 80% of the SGD 4.50 fee in force = SGD 3.60 (the figure EV-FARE-03109's money block reports as driver_compensation), the residual 20% being the platform service fee. The anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 2 (below 4) and 2/74 = 0.027 (below 0.08), and the clause needs both limbs. Under POL-GEN-03 the ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, with amount_sgd mirroring driver_compensation_sgd at SGD 3.60; the rider's SGD 4.50 charge stands and is not refunded. No clause produces a referral on these facts (the false-arrival and anti-farming routes are not triggered). The monetary effect, SGD 3.60, is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold in POL-GEN-05, so it executes automatically; either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
